1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,470
Welcome to Manham Port, where a thousand years of history are brought to life.

2
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:11,849
All the family can enjoy a day out at Manham: visit our copper mine,

3
00:00:11,849 --> 00:00:12,980
see models of the machinery it used

4
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:18,228
have your photo taken in nineteenth-century costume,

5
00:00:18,228 --> 00:00:23,695
experience at first hand how people lived at different stages throughout history,

6
00:00:23,695 --> 00:00:27,340
and especially how children studied, worked and played.

7
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:31,658
The port of Manham is located in beautiful and peaceful countryside,

8
00:00:31,658 --> 00:00:35,300
on a bend in the great River Avon

9
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:39,508
and developed here because it's the highest navigable point of the Avon -

10
00:00:39,508 --> 00:00:42,648
boats can go no higher up this river -

11
00:00:42,648 --> 00:00:48,320
and proved a handy place to load and unload cargo to and from the sea

12
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,890
which is over 23 miles away.

13
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:54,980
A small port was already established here when

14
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:57,533
about 900 years ago, tin was discovered nearby,

15
00:00:57,533 --> 00:01:01,640
though it wasn't until the Industrial Revolution

16
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:04,592
when a tremendous need for metals of all kinds developed,

17
00:01:04,592 --> 00:01:09,990
that Manham expanded to become one of the busiest ports in the country.

18
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:12,975
And because it was already so busy,

19
00:01:12,975 --> 00:01:15,220
prospectors began to look for other minerals

20
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:19,372
and by the end of the nineteenth century,

21
00:01:19,372 --> 00:01:24,490
lead, copper, manganese and arsenic were added to the cargos leaving Manham.

22
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:29,020
In the early days, the ores had been smelted - or processed

23
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,080
in the same area they were mined.

24
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:36,900
But, as demand grew, the smelting process required huge factory furnaces

25
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:38,909
or fires to melt the metal from the rock

26
00:01:38,909 --> 00:01:42,824
and there was not enough coal in the local area,

27
00:01:42,824 --> 00:01:47,130
so the rocks containing minerals had to be shipped long distances.

28
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:49,365
Sadly, in the twentieth century,

29
00:01:49,365 --> 00:01:52,940
the great port of Manham declined

30
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,410
and thousands of workers were forced to emigrate out of the area.

31
00:01:57,410 --> 00:02:02,800
The building at the port fell into disrepair, and the place became almost forgotten.

32
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:08,390
But then, the Manham Trust was formed to conserve the historical resources of the area.

33
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:17,410
It organised scores of local volunteers to remove undergrowth to find the original outlines of the installations.

34
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:21,288
It then brought in paid professionals to match installations

35
00:02:21,288 --> 00:02:26,890
with maps of the original port complex and to set about reconstructing it.

36
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:32,720
Today you can see the results of this ambitious programme of restoration.

37
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:37,532
The intention, and we believe this will be realised before the end of the year,

38
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:44,270
is to return Manham Port to the condition it reached at its peak as 'the greatest copper port in the country'.

39
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:49,170
But what can you do and see on your visit today?

40
00:02:49,170 --> 00:02:50,520
Here are just a few highlights

41
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:54,800
We suggest you start with the visit to the copper mine.

42
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,967
Travel on converted mining trains

43
00:02:56,967 --> 00:03:03,900
and journey into the depths of the mountain along seams once worked by hundreds of miners.

44
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:09,180
Watch out especially for the great pumping machines which rid the mine of water.

45
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:13,587
But please be warned that, like all mines, ours is very dark

46
00:03:13,587 --> 00:03:17,340
and closed in and we do say that children under five

47
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:21,300
and also dogs should NOT be taken into the mine.

48
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:26,140
The next recommended visit is to the village school.

49
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,603
While looking round the classrooms,

50
00:03:27,603 --> 00:03:30,240
take a special look at our display of games

51
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,870
which is one of the largest in the world.

52
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:38,260
And it's recommended that you time your visit to coincide with a guided tour.

53
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:41,980
This will give you the opportunity to ask lots of questions.

54
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:47,080
Near the school is the beautiful old sailing ketch called The George'.

55
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:51,110
You are welcome to board the boat and look round the cabins.

56
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:52,892
Look out for the ship's wheel

57
00:03:52,892 --> 00:03:55,240
which was missing until only five years ago

58
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:58,830
when it was dredged out of the silt by a local fisherman.

59
00:03:58,830 --> 00:04:00,740
We have no idea how it got there

60
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:05,670
but it's been polished and proudly restored to its original place on the boat.

61
00:04:05,670 --> 00:04:09,918
Please take care going down the ladders if you wish to visit the lower deck -

62
00:04:09,918 --> 00:04:12,750
we don't recommend you allow young children to use them.

63
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:18,940
So we hope you have a memorable visit to Manham Port and will tell your friends all about us.
